#@Comment A smooth spread of the thickness around its mean (a Gamma distribution).
#@Comment $P(X) \propto X^{1/\mathrm{CV}^2-1}\,e^{-X/(\mathrm{CV}^2 m)}$. {CV} - the relative width (standard deviation over mean); {mean} - the mean thickness $m$ in the unit of X (any value while λ is large). L from 0, R about $m(1 + 5\,\mathrm{CV})$.
